     {
      "text": "35-year-old male presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 4 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 6/10. Associated: weight loss, tiredness. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 1 years; Hypertension for 3 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: sulfa drugs. Family: diabetes. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
